 "$\\mathcal{X}, \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$F, G$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$1$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0006": "$F \\to G$", "MATH_0007": "$F \\to G$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$1$", "MATH_0010": "$\\phi : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0011": "$F \\to G$", "MATH_0012": "$2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-2-category-fibred-setoids}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d0a920620e99e596bd30f5002c280cc19bbb656fe2d190cc12b0070e89c76c67", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:40f776f5a8a023f6c1746b266cd2dba8e0217df2667b377da2eafe2243ee6935", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3bc9847a82f7862732951feb6d4f1b568af80c27ec8421ee2d1d6d8b7e81d575", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIf <MATH_0001> are fibred in groupoids and\nrepresentable by algebraic spaces <MATH_0002> over <MATH_0003>, then we have\n<MATHSEG_0001>-isomorphism<MATHSEG_0002>\nsee\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nMore precisely, any <MATH_0004>-morphism <MATH_0005>\ngives rise to a morphism <MATH_0006>. Conversely, given a morphism\nof sheaves <MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008> there exists a <MATH_0009>-morphism\n<MATH_0010> which gives rise to <MATH_0011>\nand which is unique up to unique <MATH_0012>-isomorphism.\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:624a47b1530c6315452feb920e0f5a6c3a2eacc6a699e817365269aca7ffb711", "unit_id": "tag:02ZV:prose-0003"}
